<h1>Lesson 4: Interactivity in Web Apps</h1>

<div style="display: inline-block; background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 12px;">Aligns to curriculum Lessons 6-8</div>

<p>This lesson prepares you to teach three curriculum lessons:</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
<p><b>Curriculum Lesson 6:</b> Interactivity in Web Apps</p>
<a href="[LESSON 6 URL]" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 6</a>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
<p><b>Curriculum Lesson 7:</b> Making a Button Respond</p>
<a href="[LESSON 7 URL]" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 7</a>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
<p><b>Curriculum Lesson 8:</b> Variables and Live Updates</p>
<a href="[LESSON 8 URL]" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 8</a>
</div>

<hr>

<p><b>In this lesson, you'll:</b></p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Explore a mock site to spot real interactivity in action</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Sort user actions from page elements</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Walk through the DOM and a live event-handler demo, piece by piece</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 6px 0;">• Practice evaluating AI-generated code like a QA Engineer</p>
<p style="margin: 0;">• Try a Web Lab practice activity yourself</p>

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #222222; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
<p><b>💡 Notice as you explore:</b> the difference between AI confidence and AI correctness, working code isn't proof that AI understood the request, and that distinction matters every time you're reading a student's AI-generated code.</p>
</div>

<hr>

